Retry WebGPU adapter/device requests so AMD and Intel GPUs can load.

ggml-webgpu required shader-f16 plus every adapter limit, then GGML_ASSERT
on a failed requestDevice. Chrome on AMD D3D12 often advertises a 4 GiB
maxBufferSize it will not grant, or picks an iGPU without f16. WASM aborted
and Sakutto fell back to CPU with no error. Request high-performance then
default then low-power; retry the device without optional features and with
capped/default limits; do not assert; set device_count only when a device exists.

See ggml-org/llama.cpp#21744, #23844 and Dawn D3D12 adapter-limit mismatches.

